Probabilistic facts like "Objects of type <XY> are plentiful in Nethack"
should be taken with a good grain of salt, as I observed in my last game
once again. The scroll of enchant weapon is the third most common random
scroll (identify:18%, light:9%, enchant weapon:8%) of all 22 scroll types
(where the five least common types have a probability of just 1.5% each).

In my last game I thoroughly explored the Dungeons of Doom, Sokoban, the
mines, and visited every Gehennom level until the VS, but did not find a
single one of those quite important[*] scrolls of enchant weapon; neither
randomly lying around, nor from death-drops, nor from chests or shops.
The first scroll[**] I encountered @T:55132 inside the Wizards tower on
its upper level, just before going to get the third invocation artifact.
If I wouldn't have found that one, umm.., "just in time", I'd even have
had to spend a wish.[***]

BTW; this was a (as usual randomly assigned) Rog-Hum-Fem-Cha game, and,
incidentally, the game before that one was a Rog-Hum-Mal-Cha, which had
been one of my fastest death ever; with only maxHP:12 he died after 107
turns killed by a falling rock trap. The margin between death and life
can be so narrow in Nethack.

Janis

[*] I was no spell-caster, so enchanting missiles and melee weapons would
be important.

[**] And it was the only one randomly generated in the whole game, which
lasted until T:57899.

[***] Two-handed melee with a set of +1/+0 weapons and 4x multi-fire with
+0 daggers is nice for the early/mid game, but lousy for the endgame.


